          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement of Proper Lorentz maps factor into a boost and a rotation: Fix an inertial frame of [[def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart]] and identify its vector coordinates with $\\mathbb R^4$ and $\\eta_0=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$. For a unit spatial vector $\\mathbf n_B$ and $\\chi\\in\\mathbb R$, define the boost $B_{\\mathbf n_B}(\\chi)$ by $B e_0=\\cosh\\chi\\,e_0+\\sinh\\chi\\,\\mathbf n_B$, $B\\mathbf n_B=\\sinh\\chi\\,e_0+\\cosh\\chi\\,\\mathbf n_B$, and $Bw=w$ for every $w$ Euclidean-orthogonal to $\\operatorname{span}(e_0,\\mathbf n_B)$. Every proper orthochronous linear Lorentz map $\\Lambda\\in SO^+(1,3)$, as defined in [[def-lorentz-map-and-lorentz-group]], admits $\\Lambda=B_{\\mathbf n_B}(\\chi)R_{\\mathbf n_R}(\\theta)$, where $R_{\\mathbf n_R}(\\theta)$ fixes the time axis and $\\mathbf n_R$, The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
