          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement of Dirac matrix identities and orthogonal energy projections: Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and use the definitions in [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]. For every $\\mu\\ge0$ and almost every $\\mathbf k$, the displayed Pauli blocks satisfy $h_D(\\mathbf k)^\\dagger=h_D(\\mathbf k)$, $h_D(\\mathbf k)^2=\\omega(\\mathbf k)^2I_4$, and $P_\\pm(\\mathbf k)$ are complementary orthogonal projections of rank two. The ranges $\\mathcal H_\\pm$ are closed separable Hilbert subspaces of $\\mathcal H_D$, and $h_D$ is self-adjoint on $D(h_D)=\\{u:\\omega u\\in\\mathcal H_D\\}$. The matrices also satisfy $\\{\\gamma^a,\\gamma^b\\}=-2\\eta^{ab}I_4$ and $\\gamma^{0\\dagger}=\\gamma^0$, $\\gamma^{j\\dagger}=-\\gamma^j$. For a unit spatial vector $\\mathbf n$, put $\\Sigma_{\\mathbf n}=\\operatorname{diag} The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
