      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-42",
        "notes": "Checked all eight current proof steps and fourteen direct suppliers. Pauli block multiplication yields Hermitian hD, hD squared=omega squared, Clifford signs and trace-two complementary projections; assigned apex values obey the same identities. Explicit rotation and boost conjugations agree with the oriented axis-angle and positive boost conventions. Real rational-box density extends to complex four-component L2 through real/imaginary parts and finite products; constant measure rescaling preserves density. Closed projected subspaces are separable using the stated Countable Choice for points in countably many nonempty basis intersections. Projected bounded-support approximants give dense maximal ±omega domains. Adjoint cutoff test yields q=±omega g, and component testing proves the finite direct-sum adjoint domain equality. Trigonometric products give unitary W, group law and derivative including the zero apex. Reader real/complex and direct-sum repairs are accepted without claim change; exact current post fingerprint verified. No routed finding or unresolved local gap."
      }
