          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement of Smeared free Dirac CAR fields and graded locality: Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]], let $\\mu\\ge0$, and use [[def-qft-dirac-projections]], [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]], and the antisymmetric Fock and CAR conventions of [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]] and [[lem-qft-fock-ccr-car]]. For $F\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb C^4)$, define $$\\widehat F(t,\\mathbf k)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}e^{-i\\mathbf k\\cdot\\mathbf x}F(t,\\mathbf x)\\,d^3\\mathbf x,\\qquad u_F(\\mathbf k)=\\int_{\\mathbb R}W_D(t,\\mathbf k)\\widehat F(t,\\mathbf k)\\,dt.$$ Then $u_F\\in\\mathcal H_D$, continuously in the Schwartz topology, and $$\\Psi(F)=c(P_+u_F)+c^\\dagger(\\overline{P_-u_F})$$ defines a bounded operator on $\\mathcal F_a(\\mathcal H_+\\oplus\\overline{\\mathcal H_-})$, antilinear in The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
