      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-42",
        "notes": "Independently checked all six current steps and eleven direct suppliers, including current CAR and scalar causal-support proofs as prerequisite context. Repeated integration by parts supplies finite Schwartz seminorm bounds and L2 continuity; W is unitary. Particle/conjugate antiparticle CAR have the correct second-variable-linear pairing and norm bound. Temporal boundary terms vanish, giving the tested Dirac equation. Plancherel with k=2pi xi gives the stated equal-time normalization. C± pairings have W(s-t), hence R=∂t Delta I-i hD Delta with the displayed phases; tested integrals converge absolutely, including the massless apex, and differentiation cannot enlarge support. Compact spacelike difference sets avoid the cone. Field-field CAR vanish through orthogonal species for every test; even-degree cross monomials commute by (-1)^(rs). Repaired nonfatal F1 conjugate-space misattribution by placing it in F2 with its exact existing Dirac-definition supplier; synchronized the three stale derivation claim labels and boundary locators without changing steps or interface. Reader substantive repairs are sound. No public interface changed in this adjudication; no consumer repair required. Outside historical referrals remain untouched. At final handoff the outside CAR Statement gained the exact def-separable-space reference in its Hilbert norm topology. Read that current Statement and the Definition: an at most countable dense subset is precisely the condition already proved for K. Refreshed this citation quote; no consumer claim or argument changed, and no outside historical finding was closed."
