      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-42",
        "notes": "Checked all eight proof paragraphs and eighteen exact direct suppliers. Conjugate antiparticle fibers with reversed spatial q preserve positive omega. Finite sums of scalar product L2 realizations justify projected tensor sectors; symmetric scalar cutoffs commute with fiber and antisymmetry projections. Unit phases and the 4|u|² bound prove one-particle and Fock strong continuity. Indicator multipliers obey every PVM axiom, including countable additivity by dominated convergence on product measures and the sector sum. Real-coordinate cutoffs prove sector maximal self-adjoint domains; sector testing proves the countable direct-sum adjoint equality and graph core. Triangle inequality yields future-cone support. For mu>0 every nonvacuum sector has energy at least mu; massless zero energy is null on all positive sectors, while nonzero projected ball sections give arbitrarily small positive spectral energy. Vacuum uniqueness is the one-dimensional vacuum range, as proved. Difference-quotient domination and Fatou prove both directions of generator-domain equality with correct spatial minus sign. Countable Choice is carried from product/tensor suppliers. No repair or decision owed for this untouched item."
      }
