      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-42",
        "notes": "Checked all seven proof paragraphs and sixteen exact direct suppliers. The generated triple subgroup has surjective projection by boost/rotation factorization; Clifford and beta identities survive products and inverses. Both P± beta shell identities and the reparameterized negative q=(omega,-k) yield the correct separate kernel covariance using invariant dnu. Unit Jacobian and inverse-adjoint spin factors preserve both polarized tested pairings, including conjugate antiparticle pairing. Compact smooth momentum spinors away from zero are dense; g(t)W(-t)u realizes uF=u, so the isometries extend onto the full ranges. Triple product order, tensor lift and insertion/contraction covariance agree. Affine pullbacks vary continuously in Schwartz seminorms; norm-one density and finite-sector approximation give strong continuity. The CAR normal-ordering induction subtracts at-most-(n-2)-degree contraction terms, isolating dense degree-n wedges, and a nonzero CAR relation supplies the identity for degree zero. This proves global graded-algebra cyclicity only. Translation phases exactly match the previous generator/PVM domains and positive spectrum; ±energy hD remains distinct. Half-angle values give sector (-1)^n and 4pi identity. Countable Choice is carried throughout; massless apex remains null. Reader repair accepted; no local proof gap or empirical claim found. At final handoff the outside CAR Statement gained the exact def-separable-space reference in its Hilbert norm topology. Read that current Statement and the Definition: an at most countable dense subset is precisely the condition already proved for K. Refreshed this citation quote; no consumer claim or argument changed, and no outside historical finding was closed."
      }
